Z||000002||CoolBlue87GT||06-29-2001||07:16 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by johnmac:<BR><B>insurance coverage available in Florida? </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I talked to my agent, we are looking into listing my 87 GT as a classic.<P>They have rates that are a lot less than regular insurance.<P>Of course there are some restrictions, vehicle must be at least 15 years old, and not used for general transportation.<P>I'm in Florida also, - watch out for those huge Town Cars & Chyrsler New Yorkers being driven around by the older crowd. They can't see us !<P>Good luck.<BR> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/CoolBlue87GT.gif"> <BR>||||reg||6
Z||000003||johnmac||06-29-2001||10:24 PM||||Which insurance company are you dealing with?<P>What is considered not for general transportation? I plan to use my car only 5 hrs per week - is this acceptable?<P>What kind of rates are you getting?<P>Please advise.<P>Thanks,<P>John MacHaffie <P>------------------<BR>John MacHaffie<BR>86GT "Yellowbird"<BR>12+ month project car<BR>johnmac@mpinet.net<BR>Winter Springs, Florida||||reg||1
Z||000004||TRiAD||06-29-2001||11:01 PM||||2 things...<P><B>1) A V O I D   P R O G R E S S I V E   L I K E   T H E   P L A G U E  !!!!!!<P>2) You get what you pay for.</B><P>Good luck. <P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000005||johnmac||06-29-2001||11:56 PM||||Right On Triad!<P>I had Progressive for 1 year and never again!<P>My plans is to have the cheapest insurance out there to somewhat cover my min. investment in my Fiero GT. Bought my project car for $500 and invested some $2000 in materials so far. My Labor cost at 5 cents per hour is - - well we all know how that goes.<P>I am not anticipating a full value replacement coverage.<P>------<P>Another subject <P>TRIAD Body Modifications - WOW!!!!<BR>How far along are you on the panel work and do you plan to sell kits? I be interested.<P>Thanks for your comments.<P>John||||reg||1
Z||000006||sjp777||06-30-2001||12:16 AM||||I have Nationwide.<P>$60 a month, full coverage with a $250 deductable.<P>I was worried that the bluebook on my car was only around $4500, so I took it to a Pontiac dealer and got a written appraisal giving the car a replacement value of $7500. I called Nationwide and told them what I did. They said as long as I had it in writing they would honor that amount if it got wrecked or stolen.<P>I hope I never need it, but it's good to know I'm covered.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_4.jpg"> <BR>88GT 5sp, in desperate need of an LT1<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||TRiAD||06-30-2001||06:30 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by johnmac:<BR><B>------<P>Another subject <P>TRIAD Body Modifications - WOW!!!!<BR>How far along are you on the panel work and do you plan to sell kits? I be interested...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well....I'm still trying to buy the car.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>The aesthetics were done in photoshop (and have since been revised and cleaned up..same basic idea, just cleaner). If/when I can put it all together, I would be interested in selling parts, but they'd be fiberglass (even the nose) so I'm not sure how many people would want them. I'm sure everyone here will be notified if/when it ever happens. <P>Thanks for the compliments!<BR>[EDIT]maybe someone out there who is close to Il and can do fiberglass would be interested in making the molds off my car and making the retail end a joint venture?<P>triadtuning@hotmail.com[EDIT]<P><p>[This message has been edited by TRiAD (edited 06-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Old Lar||06-30-2001||07:53 AM||||I have Nationwide and insured "historical" insurance (10 + year old car)in New York.  The cars are insured for a stated value.  It's about $100 a month for two Fieros.  Restricted use:  Car shows, parades, to and  from repairs etc (test drives after some home fixes). So I've driven to Daytona, Carlisle, the Dells, Old Orchard Beach, Maine and my mechanical work is done in Illinois.  So I've driven the Fieros over 8000 miles this year.<P>I also have old age on my side, a clean driving record and no insurance claims in 20 years.  (A deer hit me).||||reg||1
